[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) is marked known: one bug, one fix queued. Read by tenant and by the
way each report came in, its reports describe three different problems. The queued parser fix
closes one of them.

<Callout kind="warn">
#4471 is not one issue. Each problem below has its own ticket. Do not merge new date reports into
#4471 by subject; file them under the problem they show.
</Callout>

## Where they stand

Engineering closed #4471 on 05 Oct:

| problem | outcome |
| --- | --- |
| `parser` | **fixed**: `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales` |
| `hint` | **won't fix**: booking-v3 form retired |
| `one-day` | not in the update; still open |

## The problems

The `one-day` reports are also counted under `parser`, where the desk files them by tenant.

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} issues={{ parser: 'https://github.com/enterteg/mega-s01e03-dates/issues/1', hint: 'https://github.com/enterteg/mega-s01e03-dates/issues/2', 'one-day': 'https://github.com/enterteg/mega-s01e03-dates/issues/3' }} />

### `parser`: the shared parser reads dates month first

Every tenant in #4471 writes the day first. The shared parser reads every date month first, so
7 April comes out as 4 July. This is the bug the queued fix is for. It covers every report from
the app, by email, and from booking-v2 forms.

### `hint`: booking-v3 tells day-first tenants to type month first

booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. People type what the hint says, and the form
then reads the date the tenant's way, day first. The parser fix does not touch this: the form
needs its hint to follow the tenant's locale. It covers form reports from tenants on booking-v3.

### `one-day`: bookings move by one day

Tuesday 12 May shows as Monday 11 May; one meeting lands on Tuesday in Lisbon and Monday in
Toronto; an invite arrives before the booking was made. Month and day are not swapped here, so
the parser fix will not help. These look like a time zone or daylight-saving bug and need their
own investigation. The desk had already noted them (`desk-notes.json`).

## How it got merged

- [Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on subject line. Every one of these
  reports says some version of "wrong date", so three bugs shared one ticket.
- Intake's tag (`meta.intakeTag`) guesses from the reporter's browser. It does not say which problem a
  report is; tenant and way in do.
- The ticket export overlaps: some reports are listed twice. Count each id once.

